{"availability":"available","full":"elkojo/xNotary","name":"xNotary","description":"Self-custodial notarization on Bitcoin, with eIDAS qualified signatures. No backend, no accounts; your files never leave your device.","category":"Finance","language":"TypeScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-28T09:36:53Z","updated":"2026-10-07T11:43:25Z","license":"AGPL-3.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://elkojo.github.io/xNotary/","topics":[],"demo":"https://elkojo.github.io/xNotary/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:12.264Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:12.264Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T13:19:12.264Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T11:15:24.586Z","stars":0,"forks":0},{"at":"2026-10-09T13:19:12.264Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Self-custodial notarization. Hash any file locally, timestamp it on Bitcoin, then attest the electronic signatures made over it — qualified ones included. You sign with your own tools; xNotary reads the signed file and names who signed. No accounts, no database, no backend — and no copy of your documents anywhere but your own device.","### ⚠️ Public beta — not for real use yet This build has not had a security review, and its wording has not been reviewed by a lawyer. The Czech eIDAS counsel review is a release milestone and has not happened. What it produces is nonetheless real: the digests are genuinely anchored in Bitcoin and the certificates verify with the reference OpenTimestamps client, with or without this app. So treat the software as unfinished rather than the output as fake — and don't rely on it for anything that matters.","Status. Certificate 1 and Certificate 2 both work end to end, and the interface has been rebuilt around them (v0.4.1). Remaining before release: security review, Czech eIDAS counsel review, and an onboarding pass. Neither review is a code task, and both gate the \"public beta\" label coming off. See Milestones and the post-MVP roadmap."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elkojo/xNotary/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"20ad2f12a56f303392e788c7de4e50ab47becfde6aad571a34308bd2009809e3","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:24.721Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:24.721Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Self-custodial notarization. Hash any file locally, timestamp it on Bitcoin, then attest the electronic signatures made over it — qualified ones included. You sign with your own tools; xNotary reads the signed file and names who signed. No accounts, no database, no backend — and no copy of your documents anywhere but your own device.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elkojo/xNotary/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No accounts, no database, no backend — and no copy of your documents anywhere but your own device.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elkojo/xNotary/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"account","status":"documented","text":"No accounts, no database, no server state. (Proven","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elkojo/xNotary/blob/main/README.md"},{"kind":"paid_service","status":"optional","text":"Paid services around the app — archiving, printed certificates, physical delivery — are the intended business model, and the first of them makes principle 3 false on the day it ships unless it is reworded first: the app retains nothing and needs no server; an optional archive holds only what a user explicitly sends it.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elkojo/xNotary/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"20ad2f12a56f303392e788c7de4e50ab47becfde6aad571a34308bd2009809e3","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elkojo/xNotary/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:24.722Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-07T11:15:01Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/elkojo/xNotary/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T11:15:24.723Z","hash":